  dishSprite: {fileID: 1208040086343421634, guid: dbe5bac0b22c963458f1f4116ce19a1c, type: 3}
  hDialogLines:
  - text: Hello in this level the dish we will cook is Dinuguan from Nueva Ejica.
  - text: but first a little Dinuguan, a Filipino pork blood stew
  - text: 'It has many regional versions across the country. In Nueva Ecija

      it
      is locally known as Tinumis'
  - text: 'This version likely developed as a local adaptation, using young

      tamarind
      leaves (usbong ng sampaloc)'
  - text: "instead of vinegar for sourness reflecting the province\u2019s\nabundance
      of tamarind trees."
  - text: "Over time, tinumis became a traditional home-cooked dish in Nueva Ecija,\nsymbolizing
      the region\u2019s uniquetwist on a classic Filipino favorite."
